The scripts in examples/blender/ and examples/neural-server/plugins/blender_*.py drive Blender
through its Python API (bpy). Blender's licence requires published scripts that use bpy to be
GPL-compatible, so these files are licensed GPL-2.0-or-later
(https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.html), unlike the rest of the repository (MIT).

The ts23d library never imports them: it talks to Blender only through a separate process or an
HTTP server, and these examples are not part of the npm package.
